   "kind": "text",
   "text": "Staff of Chiefs on: +plan +fable +approve. Dashboard: http://127.0.0.1:4399\n\nI read the whole repo, which is 6 files. It's a plain `node:http` router with no dependencies, tested with `node --test`. Orders are two handlers in `src/routes/orders.js`, merged into one route map in `src/server.js`.\n\n**Plan**\n\n| # | Step | Owner | Model | Parallel |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Add `src/auth.js` with `requireApiKey(handler)`. It reads the `x-api-key` header and checks it against the comma-separated `API_KEYS` env var, read on each request. The check uses `crypto.timingSafeEqual` on hashed values so it takes the same time whether a key is close or not. Requests are refused (fail closed) if `API_KEYS` is empty. A wrong or missing key gets a 401 with `{\"error\":\"unauthorized\"}`. | Lead (me) | Opus 5.5 | — |\n| 2 | Wrap `GET /orders` and `POST /orders` in `orders.js`. In `server.js`, run the auth check before reading the request body, so unauthenticated requests don't get their body read or parsed. `/users` stays public. | Lead (me) | Opus 5.5 | — |\n| 3 | Write `test/orders.test.js`: no key → 401, wrong key → 401, valid key → 200/201 on both routes, no `API_KEYS` set → 401, more than one valid key works, `/users` still open | `squad-sonnet` | Sonnet | runs alongside 4 |\n| 4 | Security review of the auth diff: timing, header handling, failing closed, anything that bypasses the check | `squad-opus` | Opus | runs alongside 3 |\n| 5 | Apply the review fixes, run `npm test`, review my own diff, add `API_KEYS` usage to the README | Lead (me) | Opus 5.5 | — |\n\n**Fable isn't in the plan.** The scope is small and well bounded, so the Opus review covers the security side. If you want a full threat model as well, I can move step 4 to `squad-fable`.\n\n**Decision for you:** the header name is `x-api-key`. I'm not supporting `Authorization: Bearer`. Tell me if you want that instead.\n\nNothing is committed unless you ask. Reply OK to build, or tell me what to change."
